Hi netters.

I do not know whether this has been discussed here before, but I have some
suggestions for the future edition of the game.

As the subject line says, how about the explosive-type weapons?  We should,
of course, keep it inside the context of the ancient game of nethack, and I
can think of a number of ways to do that.  Besides, explosives already
exist in the form of land-mine trap, so we can exploit that to extend the
use of explosive weapon to a player.

I suggest that this type of weapon should be pretty mild in most of the
cases, and I think they will still be quite useful as a tool.  
For example:

1. Throwing at the monster:
 	Will do pretty heavy damage to a monster that is hit and some
	damages to the monsters nearby.  More like hand-granade type of
	weapon (Of course, we have to come up with some cool name)  Maybe
	we could shoot it with a bow or come up with a new launcher.
	Will make a hole in the wall and break the door.
	Blessing/Cursing could effect the power of explosion.

2. Setting the bomb:
	Use something like #loot command to set the bomb.  I could think of
	two types of this kind.  First land mine will explode when someone
	steps on it, and standard bomb will go off after a certain number
	of turns.  So mine will be used as more of a weapon, whereas bomb
	can be useful as a tool to create an opening in the door/wall or
	creating lots of pits and maybe a trapdoor.
	Cursed bomb will explode when you try to loot it, thereby doing the
	damage to you and Blessed bomb will let you control when to
	activate the bomb.

3. And how about...
	While we are at it, how about petroleum fountain?  #dip lamp into
	it to fill it up, and #dip arrows to make them explosive arrows.
	Hell, shouldn't we also have empty bottles to get the potion of
	water out of fountain or sink, and potion of petreoleum out of
	petroleum fountain?  I mean, where all those bottles go after you
	quaff from it?  Maybe they get recycled... :-)

Any of the above stuffs will be very vulnerable against the fire type of
attack, or the scroll of fire, but putting it into a bag should protect
it.  I don't know you will be allowed to carry them into Hell, though.
None of the potions or scrolls catch fire in the hell, so...  Maybe we can
protect the explosives from fire by rustproofing them.

Enchanting a bomb will generally increase the power of explosion, but
blindlessly enchanting a bomb will be potentially dangerous.  For example,
when you activate +6 bomb...

A voice says, "Thou arrogant, human!!" -more-
You just activated a nuclear bomb -more-
(may include lots of graphic messages) -more-
Dungeon collapses -more-
All the creatures in the dungeon are destroyed. -more-
You die... -more-








